<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:41:59Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory, says new report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4db01feb6420ae6a3c0a28088268ccf0f3b32a085fd637b1e3e1eb96a448ad3</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:41:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877--a509ee21abbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory-says-new-report/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why US investors are snapping up Germany's famed Mittelstand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:044776afd8848d869644602bd285d4ab295db679b446668d357b5c93e6162bf1</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:41:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T09:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421--453454d6f76c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Increasing amounts of US capital are flowing into Germany's traditional industrial firms and family-owned businesses. As many business owners struggle to find successors, more companies are becoming acquisition targets.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Alberta rejects separation bid, CBC projects</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4fdd6c760bdbc465dfe6ae377b0ec541a83300690712bd7ad03a1442ab3d8f45</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:41:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T06:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-rejects-separation-bid-cbc-projects/a-79708520--59931f2b4e41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-rejects-separation-bid-cbc-projects/a-79708520?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Voters have decisively rejected a proposal to begin the legal process toward Alberta's independence, dealing a major blow to a movement driven largely by economic grievances.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australian MP seriously hurt in suspected car attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e034d8a67f563946a15987597a96b060f8f693a4176e901366d4180219294810</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:40:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T06:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-seriously-hurt-in-suspected-car-attack/a-79697660--8ec3224c2b82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-seriously-hurt-in-suspected-car-attack/a-79697660?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Helen Haines, an independent federal lawmaker, suffered severe injuries in what Australia's prime minister has called a deliberate attack by a man in a car.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria seeks suspects in Germany after Starlink sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b37a52bab194f6232d5aee9842eb9fc90732265bc37f849d6241faf20f990f4b</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:40:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745--e11bc2352fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Bulgarian court has issued arrest warrants for two young German nationals suspected of setting fire to Starlink antennas. The case is reminiscent of another in Poland, which Warsaw says was orchestrated by Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Alberta votes on holding independence referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3576b185a6d39fc721d550601d7b89d5fe0d22677820517a6ae2925dfa08c55e</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:40:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-votes-on-holding-independence-referendum/a-79700283--4cfaa44e1aaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-votes-on-holding-independence-referendum/a-79700283?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canada's oil-rich western province of Alberta is not deemed likely to vote in favor of a real breakaway plebiscite. Nevertheless the separatist movement hopes to gain leverage over Mark Carney's government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can diplomacy stop another Ethiopia-Eritrea war?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:caefabe41217f15501f5a15ae53396c20d1ac196c71fa8abbb2bcf0ee67598a4</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:40:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-diplomacy-stop-another-ethiopia-eritrea-war/a-79705435--b90ab4301994.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-diplomacy-stop-another-ethiopia-eritrea-war/a-79705435?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia has installed a new administration in conflict-hit Tigray after federal forces pushed back Tigrayan fighters. But tensions with Eritrea continue to raise fears of a wider regional war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio visits India with a trip to the world's largest oil refinery topping the agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43b0561b6179805c15a32437d5f163d7ea6f258e8ab9e2ab620e96c3822a500f</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:40:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rubio-visits-india-with-a-trip-to-the-world-s-largest-oil-refinery-topping-the-agenda/a-79699826--dd280f73407c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rubio-visits-india-with-a-trip-to-the-world-s-largest-oil-refinery-topping-the-agenda/a-79699826?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A visit to India this week by Washington's top diplomat will skip New Delhi and instead include the world's largest oil refinery, which processes massive amounts of Russian crude. Is Trump looking for a new deal?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar refugees find hope in Thailand's work program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:289332c77af63c7efcf204506f2caf599f86d552a33f10e024575bdd345cbe1e</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:40:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921--572ae4634b5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Thailand granted long-staying refugees from Myanmar the right to work legally. Refugees and rights groups welcome the move but say the program's first year has exposed significant shortcomings.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>From delivery driver to global fame: A Korean writer's journey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ed6e872a9c61d1cf0259ddf0e657d50c79005454587bfe98c635f7448087c95</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:40:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-delivery-driver-to-global-fame-a-korean-writer-s-journey/a-79672757--a579002c20b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-delivery-driver-to-global-fame-a-korean-writer-s-journey/a-79672757?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">You Yeong-Gwang's The Rainfall Market tells the story of a mysterious, hidden shop that only opens when it rains. For a debut novel by an unknown author, it was a massive success.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Deepfakes, bots and distrust: How AI is shaping Israel's election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a47f7d4b4bfd98ef5ef97f0f55eb0b334a7bca564b63da9d06b21087f203fbd1</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:40:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T08:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/deepfakes-bots-and-distrust-how-ai-is-shaping-israel-s-election/a-79657988--dfb913004f7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/deepfakes-bots-and-distrust-how-ai-is-shaping-israel-s-election/a-79657988?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time, AI is playing a major role in Israel's elections. Observers warn that deepfakes, bots and influence campaigns could sway voters.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What Earth's sixth mass extinction event means for humans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23dab582121162ffddbe9b6eb468fed135a0d0eb8074e988b2965e06d177f679</id><updated>2026-10-20T13:40:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-earth-s-sixth-mass-extinction-event-means-for-humans/a-79680410--0a12d110aea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-earth-s-sixth-mass-extinction-event-means-for-humans/a-79680410?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Human activity is driving plants and animals to extinction at an unprecedented rate. As countries meet in Armenia to discuss ways to reverse nature loss, DW reveals how declining biodiversity is already harming people.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
